# Form Input Standards

All Vuetify input components must use **compact density** and **hide-details="auto"**.

## Required Props

| Prop | Value |
|------|-------|
| `density` | `"compact"` |
| `hide-details` | `"auto"` |
| `variant` | `"outlined"` |
| `autocomplete` | Always set — see table below |

## Autocomplete (HTML tokens only)

Use the standard `autocomplete` attribute on `v-text-field` / `PasswordField`. **Do not** use readonly-until-focus, hidden decoy inputs, or other autofill hacks.

| Context | Username / text | Password |
|---------|-----------------|----------|
| Login | `username` | `current-password` |
| Create user, source credentials, other non-session secrets | `off` | `new-password` |
| Change password (current) | — | `current-password` |
| Change password (new / confirm) | — | `new-password` |
| All other fields | `off` | — |

Browsers ignore `autocomplete="off"` on password fields; `new-password` is the correct token so login credentials are not filled into admin/create forms.

Login may use `density="comfortable"` for accessibility.

## Password Fields

Never use a raw `type="password"` field. Every password input uses `frontend/src/components/common/PasswordField.vue`:

- Hidden by default, with an `append-inner` eye toggle (`mdi-eye` / `mdi-eye-off`)
- Accessible `aria-label`: `Show password` / `Hide password`
- Pass through `label`, `autocomplete`, `density`, `variant`

## Duration Fields

Durations are stored in milliseconds. Always label the unit explicitly — `Dwell time (seconds)`, not `Dwell time`.

## Layout

- Do **not** use `v-row`/`v-col`, anywhere. Column gutters fight `mb-4`.
- Side-by-side fields: the `field-row` theme class. Children split the width; cap a narrow
  one with `style="max-width: …px"`; give a trailing icon cluster `field-row__actions`.
  Never add `mb-4 mb-sm-0` to a child — the class gaps both axes already.
- Button / chip clusters: `d-flex align-center flex-wrap` + `style="gap: 8px"`.
- Switch clusters: `d-flex align-center flex-wrap switch-cluster` (theme: 16px gap + non-shrinking switches).

## Switches

Boolean settings use **`v-switch` with `inset`**:

```vue
<v-switch
  v-model="enabled"
  label="Enabled"
  color="primary"
  inset
  density="compact"
  hide-details="auto"
/>
```

Do not use `v-checkbox` for on/off settings rows.
